---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Prototypes"
  description="Exploratory developer tooling prototypes for CI build duration analysis and game engine crash log triage."
>
  <!-- ============================================================
       HEADER & MASTHEAD
       ============================================================ -->
  <header class="proto-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Developer Tooling &middot; Exploratory Prototypes</p>
    <div class="wayrule" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <h1 class="display h1">Build logs and crash reports</h1>
    <p class="tagline">Two prototypes tested on synthetic data</p>

    <p class="lede">I built two prototypes: one analyzes CI build durations and timeouts, and the other groups game engine crash logs and suggests related source changes. I tested both with synthetic data.</p>

    <div class="disclaimer-banner" role="note">
      <div class="disclaimer-badge">Prototype Context</div>
      <p class="disclaimer-text">These prototypes test log parsing, stack normalization, and rules for locating possible faults. They have not been evaluated on production data and are not published research.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- ============================================================
       1. ENGINEERING PILLARS & BACKGROUND
       ============================================================ -->
  <h2 class="sec-label">
    01 / Background
    <span>CS Degree &middot; Ubisoft Game Dev &middot; Toolchain Automation</span>
  </h2>

  <div class="triad-grid">
    <!-- Pillar 1: Computer Science Degree & Academics -->
    <article class="triad-card">
      <div>
        <div class="triad-header">
          <p class="triad-number">01</p>
          <h3 class="triad-title display">Bachelor of Computer Science</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="triad-body">I graduated from <strong>Dalhousie University with a GPA of 3.92</strong> and was recognized as a Sexton Scholar and on the Dean’s List. My degree included certificates in Cybersecurity and Web/Mobile Systems.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="triad-pills" aria-label="Academic credentials">
        <li>Dalhousie University</li>
        <li>GPA 3.92</li>
        <li>Sexton Scholar</li>
        <li>Systems Architecture</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <!-- Pillar 2: Game Industry Engineering Experience -->
    <article class="triad-card">
      <div>
        <div class="triad-header">
          <p class="triad-number">02</p>
          <h3 class="triad-title display">Game Industry Experience</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="triad-body">During my <strong>gameplay programming co-op at Ubisoft Halifax</strong>, I worked with Unity, C#, Cinemachine cameras, and AI behavior trees. That gave me experience with game development tools and debugging.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="triad-pills" aria-label="Game development stack">
        <li>Ubisoft Halifax</li>
        <li>Unity &amp; C#</li>
        <li>Asset Pipelines</li>
        <li>Engine Debugging</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <!-- Pillar 3: Toolchain Automation -->
    <article class="triad-card">
      <div>
        <div class="triad-header">
          <p class="triad-number">03</p>
          <h3 class="triad-title display">Developer Toolchain Automation</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="triad-body">I use Python and .NET 8 for tools that parse logs, normalize stack frames, and explore possible connections between failures and source changes.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="triad-pills" aria-label="Toolchain proficiency">
        <li>Python &amp; .NET 8</li>
        <li>Log Ingestion</li>
        <li>AST Analysis</li>
        <li>CI Automation</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       2. PROTOTYPE 01: CI TIMEOUT & DURATION ANALYZER
       ============================================================ -->
  <h2 class="sec-label">
    02 / Prototype: CI Build Duration &amp; Timeout Analyzer
    <span>Python &middot; scikit-learn &middot; Log Segmentation</span>
  </h2>

  <div class="proto-card">
    <div class="proto-grid">
      <div class="proto-col">
        <h3 class="proto-heading">What was built</h3>
        <p class="proto-text">A Python tool that splits build logs into asset cooking, shader compilation, C++ compilation, and linking phases. It uses Random Forest regression to explore relationships between phase durations, asset changes, and timeouts.</p>

        <h3 class="proto-heading">Synthetic data used</h3>
        <p class="proto-text">I generated hundreds of simulated build runs with different asset change volumes, shader cache miss rates, and dependency graph depths to test parsing and model fitting.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="proto-col">
        <h3 class="proto-heading">What I was trying to learn</h3>
        <p class="proto-text">I wanted to see whether logs could be split into phases without custom build-system hooks, and whether slower early phases could help predict later timeouts.</p>

        <h3 class="proto-heading">What I would test next</h3>
        <p class="proto-text">Real CI logs from a game engine such as Godot or a large C++ project would let me test the approach against differences in runner hardware, cache behavior, and network delays.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <ul class="proto-features" aria-label="Key features of CI analyzer">
      <li>Log phase segmentation for asset baking, compilation, and linking stages.</li>
      <li>Feature extraction on asset delta volume and dependency graph modifications.</li>
      <li>Threshold-based early warning heuristics for pipeline timeouts.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       3. PROTOTYPE 02: GAME ENGINE CRASH LOG TRIAGE
       ============================================================ -->
  <h2 class="sec-label">
    03 / Prototype: Game Engine Crash Log Triage
    <span>.NET 8 (C#) &middot; Stack Normalization &middot; Fault Localization</span>
  </h2>

  <div class="proto-card">
    <div class="proto-grid">
      <div class="proto-col">
        <h3 class="proto-heading">What was built</h3>
        <p class="proto-text">A .NET 8 command-line tool that removes changing memory addresses and thread identifiers from crash logs. It uses SHA-256 signatures to group similar stacks and applies rules to connect stack frames with recent Git changes.</p>

        <h3 class="proto-heading">Synthetic data used</h3>
        <p class="proto-text">I used 50 synthetic logs covering six failure types: broken NodePaths after scene changes, null physics bodies, shader buffer mismatches, disposal races during scene unload, signals sent to deleted UI elements, and navigation array overflows.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="proto-col">
        <h3 class="proto-heading">What I was trying to learn</h3>
        <p class="proto-text">I wanted to see whether removing variable details would group repeated crashes consistently, and whether matching stack frames to recently changed methods could identify the relevant commit in simulated regressions.</p>

        <h3 class="proto-heading">What I would test next</h3>
        <p class="proto-text">Real engine crash reports would let me test the tool against inlined frames, interleaved thread logs, and regressions involving more than one commit.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <ul class="proto-features" aria-label="Key features of crash triage engine">
      <li>Memory-independent stack frame normalization (stripping dynamic pointers to canonical cluster hashes).</li>
      <li>Automated deduplication clustering across raw crash log collections (88% reduction on test fixtures).</li>
      <li>Deterministic heuristic mapping from call stack frames to suspect Git commits and AST changes.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <!-- Terminal Execution Demonstration -->
  <div class="terminal-wrapper" role="region" aria-label="Crash Triage Engine Execution Log">
    <div class="terminal-header">
      <div class="terminal-controls" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="control-dot dot-red"></span>
        <span class="control-dot dot-yellow"></span>
        <span class="control-dot dot-green"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="terminal-title">godot_triage_engine.exe &middot; Terminal Output</div>
      <div class="terminal-badge">ILLUSTRATIVE OUTPUT &middot; SYNTHETIC DATA</div>
    </div>

    <pre class="terminal-content"><code><span class="t-banner">===========================================================================
    EXPLORATORY GAME ENGINE CRASH LOG TRIAGE & FAULT LOCALIZATION ENGINE
           Synthetic Fixture Pipeline & Stack NormalIZATION Demo
===========================================================================</span>

<span class="t-step">[Step 1/4]</span> Ingesting raw C# crash log fixtures (simulated game-engine failure modes)...
 <span class="t-success">&rarr;</span> Ingested 50 synthetic crash logs with dynamic memory addresses and timestamps.

<span class="t-step">[Step 2/4]</span> Executing memory-independent stack frame normalization & SHA-256 deduplication...
 <span class="t-success">&rarr;</span> Formed 6 unique crash clusters from 50 raw logs.
 <span class="t-success">&rarr;</span> Normalized dynamic pointers across all frames into canonical cluster hashes.

<span class="t-step">[Step 3/4]</span> Running heuristic fault localization & Git commit mapping on simulated fixtures...
   * <span class="t-cluster">[CLUSTER_01] NodePath Resolution Failure (Scene Reparenting)</span>
     - Exception  : <span class="t-file">System.NullReferenceException</span>
     - Occurrences: 9 logs (18.0%)
     - Suspect Commit: <span class="t-commit">a3f89b1c7d...</span> ("refactor(scene): move WeaponHolder node under CharacterRig hierarchy")
     - File & Method : <span class="t-file">Source/Combat/WeaponController.cs &rarr; GameEngine.Core.Combat.WeaponController._Ready()</span>
     - Root Cause    : Stale NodePath string literal in WeaponController._Ready(). Hierarchy was refactored, moving WeaponHolder under CharacterRig without updating the path constant.

   * <span class="t-cluster">[CLUSTER_02] Null PhysicsDirectBodyState3D Reference in _PhysicsProcess</span>
     - Exception  : <span class="t-file">System.NullReferenceException</span>
     - Occurrences: 9 logs (18.0%)
     - Suspect Commit: <span class="t-commit">c4d7e2a9b8...</span> ("feat(physics): implement asynchronous raycast sweep for character movement")
     - File & Method : <span class="t-file">Source/Physics/PlayerCharacter3D.cs &rarr; GameEngine.Core.Physics.PlayerCharacter3D._PhysicsProcess(Double delta)</span>
     - Root Cause    : Missing null check on KinematicCollision3D.GetCollider(). Asynchronous raycasts and concurrent body despawns leave the collider reference null upon slide resolution.

   * <span class="t-cluster">[CLUSTER_03] Shader Uniform Buffer Layout Binding Mismatch</span>
     - Exception  : <span class="t-file">Engine.GraphicsException</span>
     - Occurrences: 8 logs (16.0%)
     - Suspect Commit: <span class="t-commit">f9a8b7c6d5...</span> ("feat(rendering): add chromatic aberration and vignette compute shader")
     - File & Method : <span class="t-file">Source/Rendering/CustomPostProcessPipeline.cs &rarr; GameEngine.Rendering.CustomPostProcessPipeline.CreateComputePipeline()</span>
     - Root Cause    : UniformSet layout descriptor mismatch at binding index 2. Compute shader was updated to require a new uniform buffer, but UniformSetCreate was passed an outdated descriptor array.

   * <span class="t-cluster">[CLUSTER_04] Multi-Threaded RenderingServer Race Condition on Scene Unload</span>
     - Exception  : <span class="t-file">System.ObjectDisposedException</span>
     - Occurrences: 8 logs (16.0%)
     - Suspect Commit: <span class="t-commit">e1f2a3b4c5...</span> ("perf(world): offload voxel chunk mesh generation to background Task workers")
     - File & Method : <span class="t-file">Source/World/ChunkRenderer.cs &rarr; GameEngine.World.ChunkRenderer.AsyncMeshUpdateWorker()</span>
     - Root Cause    : Cross-thread Object disposal race condition. ChunkRenderer dispatches async background Task workers that access engine pointers while the main thread frees chunks during scene unloading.

   * <span class="t-cluster">[CLUSTER_05] Signal Emission to Disposed UI Callable Target</span>
     - Exception  : <span class="t-file">Engine.SignalException</span>
     - Occurrences: 8 logs (16.0%)
     - Suspect Commit: <span class="t-commit">b2c3d4e5f6...</span> ("ui(hud): recreate player health bar widget on scene respawn")
     - File & Method : <span class="t-file">Source/Gameplay/HealthComponent.cs &rarr; GameEngine.Gameplay.HealthComponent.ApplyDamage(Single amount)</span>
     - Root Cause    : Signal emission to a stale Callable on a disposed UI instance. HealthComponent emits HealthChanged to a widget queued for deletion without unhooking signal handlers.

   * <span class="t-cluster">[CLUSTER_06] NavigationAgent3D Empty Path Waypoint Index Overflow</span>
     - Exception  : <span class="t-file">System.IndexOutOfRangeException</span>
     - Occurrences: 8 logs (16.0%)
     - Suspect Commit: <span class="t-commit">d8e9f01a2b...</span> ("ai(navigation): optimize waypoint path stepping for patrol agents")
     - File & Method : <span class="t-file">Source/AI/EnemyNavigationController.cs &rarr; GameEngine.AI.EnemyNavigationController.GetNextSteeringVector()</span>
     - Root Cause    : IndexOutOfRangeException in EnemyNavigationController. Path query returned an empty Vector3 array during dynamic navigation mesh rebaking, causing an unchecked index [0] access.

<span class="t-step">[Step 4/4]</span> Exporting structured triage results to JSON artifact...
 <span class="t-success">&rarr;</span> Structured triage results saved to: <span class="t-file">'triage_engine_results.json'</span>

<span class="t-banner">===========================================================================
               TRIAGE ENGINE EXECUTION COMPLETE
===========================================================================</span>
 Total Simulated Logs Processed  : <span class="t-accent">50</span>
 Unique Crash Clusters Isolated  : <span class="t-accent">6</span>
 Deduplication Normalization Rate: <span class="t-success">88.0%</span>
 Heuristic Commit Matches        : <span class="t-success">6/6 archetypes localized</span>
 Generated Output Artifact       : <span class="t-file">triage_engine_results.json</span>
<span class="t-banner">===========================================================================</span></code></pre>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .h1 { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5.5vw, 3.4rem); margin-top: var(--space-1); }
  .proto-hero { margin-top: var(--space-1); }
  .tagline {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--cobalt);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 72ch;
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  /* Disclaimer Banner */
  .disclaimer-banner {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    background: var(--paper-panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--cobalt);
    padding: var(--space-3);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
  .disclaimer-badge {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.625rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    background: var(--cobalt);
    color: var(--paper);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    white-space: nowrap;
    margin-top: 1px;
  }
  .disclaimer-text {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .sec-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-1);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .sec-label span {
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  /* Triad Grid */
  .triad-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .triad-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  .triad-card {
    background: var(--paper-panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: var(--space-4);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    position: relative;
  }
  .triad-card::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 3px;
    background: var(--rule);
    transition: background-color 0.2s ease;
  }
  .triad-card:hover::before {
    background: var(--cobalt);
  }
  .triad-number {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--cobalt);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
  .triad-title {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
  }
  .triad-body {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .triad-pills {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px;
    margin-top: auto;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .triad-pills li {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    padding: 3px 9px;
  }

  /* Prototype Cards */
  .proto-card {
    background: var(--paper-panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }
  .proto-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .proto-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  .proto-col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  .proto-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--cobalt);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    margin-bottom: 2px;
  }
  .proto-heading:first-of-type {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .proto-text {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .proto-features {
    list-style: none;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: var(--space-3) 0 0;
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
  }
  .proto-features li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 14px;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .proto-features li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.55em;
    width: 5px;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--cobalt);
  }

  /* Terminal Execution Block */
  .terminal-wrapper {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    background: #14161B;
    color: #E2E8F0;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
  }
  .terminal-header {
    background: #1F232B;
    padding: 10px 16px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #2D333F;
  }
  .terminal-controls {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
  }
  .control-dot {
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .dot-red { background: #FF5F56; }
  .dot-yellow { background: #FFBD2E; }
  .dot-green { background: #27C93F; }
  .terminal-title {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: #94A3B8;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .terminal-badge {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.625rem;
    background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.15);
    color: #38BDF8;
    border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.4);
    padding: 2px 8px;
  }
  .terminal-content {
    padding: var(--space-3);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    overflow-x: auto;
    max-height: 480px;
    overflow-y: auto;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .t-banner { color: #60A5FA; font-weight: bold; }
  .t-step { color: #FCD34D; font-weight: 600; }
  .t-success { color: #4ADE80; }
  .t-cluster { color: #38BDF8; font-weight: 600; }
  .t-commit { color: #F472B6; }
  .t-file { color: #A78BFA; }
  .t-accent { color: #38BDF8; }
</style>
